sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Priya as Priya (MDM analyst)
    participant PUB as MDM brain: SAP publisher
    participant SL as SAP B1 Service Layer (/b1s/v2)
    participant AUD as Audit log

    Priya->>PUB: Publish the approved request
    PUB->>SL: POST /Login {CompanyDB, UserName, Password}
    SL-->>PUB: 200 SessionId, cookies B1SESSION + ROUTEID
    PUB->>AUD: sap_call: Login (password never logged)
    PUB->>SL: POST /BusinessPartners {CardCode, ..., Frozen: tYES}
    SL-->>PUB: 201 Created, record exists but is inactive
    PUB->>AUD: sap_call: POST (bank fields masked)
    PUB->>SL: GET /BusinessPartners('C00123')
    SL-->>PUB: 200 the record as SAP stored it
    PUB->>AUD: sap_call: GET
    Note right of PUB: Compare every field sent with every field read back
    alt every field matches
        PUB->>SL: PATCH /BusinessPartners('C00123') {Frozen: tNO}
        SL-->>PUB: 204 No Content, record is now active
        PUB->>AUD: sap_call: PATCH
    else a field differs
        PUB-->>Priya: Record left inactive, the differing fields are shown
    end
    PUB->>SL: POST /Logout
    PUB->>AUD: sap_call: Logout
    PUB-->>Priya: Read-back table: field, sent, stored in SAP, match
    Note over PUB,AUD: A 401 (session expired) means one fresh Login, then the same call is repeated once. If an audit row cannot be written, publishing stops.
